---
import DocsLayout from "../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";

const githubActionsSnippet = `- name: Build providers
  run: |
    go build -o bin/considered ./cmd/considered
    go build -o bin/considered-scc ./cmd/considered-scc

- name: Considered check
  run: |
    PATH="\${GITHUB_WORKSPACE}/bin:\${PATH}" bin/considered check`;
---

<DocsLayout
  title="CI"
  description="Use Considered in CI and code scanning workflows."
  current="/ci/"
>
  <article class="doc">
    <h1>CI</h1>
    <p>
      Considered exits non-zero only for violations or usage/configuration
      errors. Variances and warnings stay visible without failing the check.
    </p>

    <h2>Exit codes</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Code</th>
          <th>Meaning</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td><code>0</code></td>
          <td>All checks pass.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>1</code></td>
          <td>One or more violations.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td><code>2</code></td>
          <td>Usage or configuration error.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>

    <h2>Machine-readable output</h2>
    <pre><code>considered check --json
considered check --sarif</code></pre>

    <p>
      In SARIF, violations are emitted as errors, warnings as warnings, and
      variances as informational notes.
    </p>

    <h2>GitHub Actions</h2>
    <pre><code>{githubActionsSnippet}</code></pre>
  </article>
</DocsLayout>
